  "resource": {
    "body": "<div>\n            \n  <div class=\"section\">\n\n<p>Zotonic has built-in support for HTTPS and TLS (previously SSL) certificate\nhandling.</p>\n<p>All sites share a single TLS port using Server Name Indication for\nvirtual hosting and certificate selection.</p>\n<p>The following guides are useful:</p>\n<dl class=\"docutils\">\n<dt><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"/id/doc_developerguide_deployment_privilegedports#guide-deployment-privilegedports\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Running on Port 80 and Port 443</span></a></dt>\n<dd>Let connect to the default https (443) and http (80) ports.</dd>\n<dt><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"/id/doc_developerguide_configuration_port_ssl_configuration#ref-port-ssl-configuration\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Port configurations</span></a></dt>\n<dd>Configure all Zotonic listen ports, depending on your server configuration\nand proxy usage.</dd>\n<dt><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"/id/doc_developerguide_deployment_nginx#guide-deployment-nginx\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">Proxying Zotonic with nginx</span></a></dt>\n<dd>If you want to use nginx as a terminating proxy for SSL connections.</dd>\n<dt><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"/id/doc_module_mod_ssl_letsencrypt\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">mod_ssl_letsencrypt</span></a></dt>\n<dd>Automatically fetch free SSL certificates from Let’s Encrypt.</dd>\n<dt><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"/id/doc_module_mod_ssl_ca\"><span class=\"std std-ref\">mod_ssl_ca</span></a></dt>\n<dd>Use SSL certificates obtained from a Certificate Authority.</dd>\n</dl>\n</div>\n\n\n           </div>",
